## Context

The accepted migration baseline `mvp-baseline-0761.zip` is immutable, while the
canonical observatory JSON is explicitly a later local preview that precedes a
release extension.  The compatibility test currently conflates those contracts
by requiring every live preview view to remain byte-identical to the baseline.
The same refresh added two reviewed ZAF claims and one documented dry search,
making the ZAF migration's literal 1,084-row assertion stale at 1,087.

## First test

The existing full-gate failures are the red tests:
`tests/test_jetp_compatibility.py::test_all_mvp_views_match_authoritative_builder_and_frozen_baseline`
for five refreshed views and
`tests/test_jetp_zaf_migration.py::test_zaf_candidate_reconciles_inventory_legacy_and_unchanged_views`.

## Actions and exit criteria

- [ ] Live MVP views remain exactly equal to the authoritative builder output.
- [ ] The 0761 archive remains independently pinned by its recorded byte size
      and SHA-256; no recapture or mutation is permitted.
- [ ] The ZAF migration expects all 1,087 currently retained legacy rows while
      preserving per-table assertions and pinning the refreshed 509,315-byte
      canonical preview payload.
- [ ] Targeted tests and `make check-fast` pass.  The unrelated 0829 module-size
      lint remains owned by its existing worktree and is not changed here.

